  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Isolated to scattered showers today.\n\n-  A system tonight will cause moderate travel impacts mainly\n   south of the Highway 12 corridor.\n\n-  Another round of light valley snow Sunday night into Monday.\n\n\nA few showers will continue to linger across the Northern Rockies\ntoday. The next pulse of moisture is still on track to push across\nthe regional late this afternoon into the overnight hours. Snow\nlevels will start off around 6000 feet and lower to around 4000\nfeet by Saturday morning. The bulk of the precipitation appears to\nbe across north central Idaho into southwest Montana. Winter\nweather advisories have been issued for the areas that are\nexpected to receive the biggest impact from snow. Georgetown Lake, Lolo\nand Lost Trail passes are expected to receive up to 6 inches of \nnew snow. While Butte, MacDonald and Homestake passes are\nanticipated to receive between 2 to 5 inches of snow by Saturday\nmorning. \n\nA transitory ridge of high pressure slides over the region on\nSaturday into Sunday morning causing a respite in the\nprecipitation. Then another low pressure system is expected to\npush into the Northern Rockies late Sunday in Monday. An active\nweather pattern is expected to remain over the Northern Rockies\nthrough the remainder of next week.",
